  "hypothesis": "H: Given a completed structured planner answer and a newer typed health/ammo sample, current V39 final admission first returns READY_FOR_ACTION_VALIDITY. Recomputable V2 action validity then allows current signals to reach fresh Executor admission, after which an actual InputOwner keydown can be bound to first acceptance; if health falls below the authored envelope, admission rejects before any keydown.",
  "test": "T: Two arms from retained typed seq2→seq3 with retained health/ammo values, and capture epochs rebased into current perf_counter monotonic domain (source age 200ms, current age initially 20ms): health=97 current control and synthetic health=80 drop (source=97, authored maximum loss=8, hard minimum=89). Because original frame binding names a different desktop window, both source/current typed bindings are explicitly rebound to the focused Xvfb test window with geometry [0,0,320,200]. A deterministic completed planner answer passes through AST-extracted current-main final_admission_from_planner_result, prepare_action_admission and bind_first_plan_acceptance. In the valid arm only, current-main V4/V12 owner produces XTest keydown after VALID_CURRENT, records first acceptance, then explicit verified keyup. In the invalid arm no input is issued. One candidate invocation total.",
  "decision": "D: PASS_METHOD_SCOPED only if the control reaches READY_FOR_ACTION_VALIDITY then VALID_CURRENT/READY_FOR_FRESH_EXECUTOR_ADMISSION then observed Xvfb KeyPress and INPUT_ADMITTED receipt, followed by owner-verified X keyup; and health-drop reaches REJECTED_ACTION_NOT_CURRENT with no input admission, KeyPress, or executor acceptance; both owners stop and Xvfb exits 0. Any mismatch is STOP.",
  "confounds": "C: Health=80 is synthetic from retained observation metadata. Window bindings are synthetic and point to the Xvfb fixture, not the retained game window. Fake planner and accepted-executor response are deterministic protocol fixtures, not model or production executor subprocess. Xvfb server/observer and InputOwner are real, but no game or physical device exists.",
